  "uncovered_crash_windows": [
    "The deterministic race test mocks Popen and the child process; the OS kill/reap path was not run against a real child or Kaggle process in this turn.",
    "The local server may accept or execute a request before cancellation; delivery remains unknown and there is no receipt reconciliation or idempotency key.",
    "If kill/reap is not confirmed by the send deadline, the persisted state remains pending; a later spawn is killed before request bytes are written, but an indefinitely stalled Popen call cannot be forcibly cancelled before it returns.",
    "Process loss after F response persistence but before HF begins leaves no resume path; any attempt journal blocks replay.",
    "SIGKILL, machine/power loss, disk-full behavior, torn JSONL, partial request writes, fsync faults, and cross-host flock were not tested.",
    "Post-readback mutation of the working copy before runpy opens it is not prevented by an immutable mount or file-descriptor execution path.",
    "Real backend/model artifact hashes, schema support, deployment state, and output quality remain unverified."
  ],
  "review_findings_from_v4": [
    {
      "finding": "Child EOF could pass an empty request to the local generation endpoint.",
      "v5_change": "Worker validates stdin as nonempty JSON with a nonempty messages array before constructing a request or calling urlopen.",
      "regression": "Empty and malformed input cases assert SystemExit and no mocked urlopen call."
    },
    {
      "finding": "A reaped process could be marked terminated even when kill() was not requested.",
      "v5_change": "A shared predicate requires both kill_requested and reaped; all sender cleanup paths retain and pass both values.",
      "regression": "Pure local predicate test covers both required and missing conditions."
    }
  ]
